From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:17:06 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 263/297] Meridian: Context Insights reads Codex, OpenCode,
 Qwen, Gemini and Copilot

Context Insights showed only Claude Code sessions. Now the Workbench finds
the session a terminal started for five more agents, from each one's own
record on this computer, and the same analysis runs on it: the context and
its window, tokens over time with the cause of each spike, heavy tool
results, rereads, compactions, a cold cache.

- Codex: ~/.codex/sessions/.../rollout-*.jsonl (token_usage_record, or
  token_count in older versions; window; the ChatGPT plan's limits).
- Qwen Code: ~/.qwen/projects/<root>/chats/*.jsonl (usageMetadata,
  contextWindowSize, chat_compression).
- Gemini CLI: ~/.gemini/tmp/<project>/chats/session-*.jsonl (records by
  id, last one wins, $rewindTo drops; the CLI's window table).
- Copilot CLI: ~/.copilot/session-state/<id>/events.jsonl
  (session.usage_record with maxPromptTokens).
- OpenCode 1.x: opencode.db opened read-only (step-finish parts with each
  step's cost; subagent child sessions; models.dev cache for the window
  and prices).
A terminal's session: the newest one begun in the project between its
start and the next same-agent terminal's, else one resumed in it. Prices
only where the agent records them (OpenCode); elsewhere tokens, labelled.
Amp, Cursor, Droid, Goose and sandboxes answer with the reason they are
not readable instead of another agent's session.

Formats were checked against the real CLIs (Codex 0.163, Qwen Code
0.28.4, Gemini CLI 0.71.1, Copilot CLI 1.0.103, OpenCode 1.2.6) run with
a temp HOME against a local stand-in model; the fixtures come from those
sessions with paths scrubbed. --meridian-agent-home points tests at
their own agents' homes.

